&lt;p&gt;The Customer Advocacy Marketing Manager owns both the strategy and scaled production of customer proof-point content: case studies, customer quotes and testimonials, logo usage and compliance, and the customer reviews program (G2, Gartner Peer Insights, TrustRadius). This role also owns the Customer Awards program, on-site customer content capture (video/filming) at flagship events, and the review-platform vendor relationships and budget. The ideal candidate can set a proof-point content roadmap and prioritize it against business impact, not just execute a queue — while also running a high-volume content operation end-to-end, from sourcing through legal and customer approval. This role partners closely with our Senior Manager who owns high-touch programs like our CAB, Executive Sponsorship, RKO, and customer community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in customer marketing, content marketing, or marketing operations, with demonstrated ownership of both strategy and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of setting a content roadmap and prioritizing initiatives against business impact, not just delivering against an intake queue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of owning content projects end-to-end, including legal/compliance coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning vendor relationships and budget, ideally for review-generation or reference platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication skills and an eye for turning customer insight into compelling assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CRM systems (e.g., Salesforce) and content intelligence tools (e.g., Peerbound, Gong) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable managing on-site logistics for large customer-facing events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy &amp;amp; Prioritization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the annual case study and proof-point content roadmap in partnership with Product Marketing, aligned to revenue and pipeline priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine which customer stories, quotes, and proof points to pursue based on expected pipeline, bookings, and adoption impact, rather than a first-in-first-out intake queue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Content Production&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the scaled creation and end-to-end delivery of customer content — quotes, testimonials, and case studies — from sourcing through legal and customer approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use tools like Peerbound to transform customer insights from Gong calls into approved, actionable content at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the creation and promotion of customer spotlights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage updates to existing case studies and customer stories as messaging and strategy evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Reviews &amp;amp; Platform Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the customer reference database and the review-generation program across platforms including G2, Gartner Peer Insights, and TrustRadius.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own vendor relationships and budget for review platforms, including contract renewals and spend decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logo Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end process for customer logo usage, ensuring adherence to contract terms and legal/brand compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Awards Program&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the customer awards program on a recurring annual cadence: nominee sourcing, winner selection coordination, winner notification, awards production, and integration into the event schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event Content Capture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own on-site video filming and customer engagement logistics at flagship events, including building the customer filming schedule and securing signed participation agreements ahead of the event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously refine the end-to-end content workflow, from intake to publication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project manage creation, review, and approval processes for all customer proof-point assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on the performance and business impact of proof-point content (pipeline, bookings, adoption influence).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regular reporting to stakeholders and feed the consolidated advocacy narrative owned by the Advocacy Programs Senior Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain proactive communication with Sales, CS, Product Marketing, and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the point of contact and escalation path for each owned initiative; surface project risks before they affect a deadline.&lt;/li&gt;
