&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About AlphaSense:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AlphaSense is the AI platform redefining market intelligence and workflow orchestration, trusted by thousands of leading organizations to drive faster, more confident decisions in business and finance. The platform combines domain-specific AI with a vast content universe of over 500 million premium business documents — including equity research, earnings calls, expert interviews, filings, news, and internal proprietary content. Purpose-built for speed, accuracy, and enterprise-grade security, AlphaSense helps teams extract critical insights, uncover market-moving trends, and automate complex workflows with high-quality outputs. With AI solutions like Generative Search, Generative Grid, and Deep Research, AlphaSense delivers the clarity and depth professionals need to navigate complexity and obtain accurate, real-time information quickly. For more information, visit &lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.alpha-sense.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.alpha-sense.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;. Come join us.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Data team at AlphaSense is responsible for delivering the data foundation that powers our industry-leading market intelligence platform. We focus on sourcing, integrating, and surfacing structured datasets that enable clients to discover and act on insights in new ways. Our team is dedicated to delivering these datasets directly into our clients&#39; most critical workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Product Manager to own and define how our financial data is surfaced through search and agentic capabilities across the AlphaSense platform. In this role, you&#39;ll sit at the intersection of our vast financial datasets and the systems that make that data discoverable, screenable, and actionable for end users and AI agents alike. You will be responsible for understanding how financial content is structured, indexed, and ranked so that it can be reliably surfaced through search, screening, and agentic workflows, defining the product experience that makes our data foundation a trusted input for both human analysts and AI-driven research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with engineering, design, and business stakeholders to define requirements, author PRDs, and lead the development of new features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An experienced Product Manager with a minimum of 5 years of experience building SaaS products in partnership with engineering and scrum teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in financial data products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear, persuasive communicator who creates PRDs, roadmaps, and requirements that align stakeholders and drive execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and detail-oriented, with a proven ability to manage a complex product backlog and deliver features end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic thinker with a discovery mindset, deeply curious about client workflows and pain points, especially those of financial analysts, investment bankers, and corporate development/deal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning roadmap and delivery in SaaS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI-powered search or workflow technologies is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Business, or a related field required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the short- and mid-term roadmaps for how financial data is surfaced through search, screening, and agentic capabilities, aligning with business objectives and client needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the long-term Financial Data vision by building a deep understanding of client personas (e.g., analysts, bankers, corporate development professionals) and how they search, screen, and query financial content, both directly and through AI agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously assess gaps in searchability, screening logic, and content structure, and prioritize improvements to how data is tagged, indexed, and ranked to close them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and prioritize product requirements (PRDs) informed by customer discovery and client feedback, specifically related to search relevance, screening functionality, and the retrievability of financial content by agentic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering, design, and GTM teams to ensure successful product launches and adoption of new search, screening, and agentic features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with data platform and AI/ML teams to define how financial content should be structured and exposed so it can be effectively consumed by search infrastructure and agentic tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development lifecycle for new search, screening, and agentic capabilities, from ideation and user stories through to launch and post-launch iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and conduct QA strategies for search accuracy, screening precision, and the reliability of agentic retrieval over financial content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with core data platform teams to ensure seamless data delivery, indexing performance, and reliability for search, screening, and agentic use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For base compensation, we set standard ranges for all roles based on function and level benchmarked against similar stage growth companies and internal comparables. In order to be compliant with local legislation, as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, we share salary ranges on all job postings regardless of desired hiring location. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors including candidate experience/expertise and may vary from the amounts listed below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may also be offered a performance-based bonus, equity, and a generous benefits program.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$111,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$139,000 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AlphaSense is an equal-opportunity employer. We are committed to a work environment that supports, inspires, and respects all individuals. All employees share in the responsibility for fulfilling AlphaSense’s commitment to equal employment opportunity. AlphaSense does not discriminate against any employee or applicant on the basis of race, color, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, age, religion, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, military or veteran status, disability, or any other non-merit factor. This policy applies to every aspect of employment at AlphaSense, including recruitment, hiring, training, advancement, and termination.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;In addition, it is the policy of AlphaSense to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified employees who have protected disabilities to the extent required by applicable laws, regulations, and ordinances where a particular employee works.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
