&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About AlphaSense:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AlphaSense is the AI platform redefining market intelligence and workflow orchestration, trusted by thousands of leading organizations to drive faster, more confident decisions in business and finance. The platform combines domain-specific AI with a vast content universe of over 500 million premium business documents — including equity research, earnings calls, expert interviews, filings, news, and internal proprietary content. Purpose-built for speed, accuracy, and enterprise-grade security, AlphaSense helps teams extract critical insights, uncover market-moving trends, and automate complex workflows with high-quality outputs. With AI solutions like Generative Search, Generative Grid, and Deep Research, AlphaSense delivers the clarity and depth professionals need to navigate complexity and obtain accurate, real-time information quickly. For more information, visit &lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.alpha-sense.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.alpha-sense.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;. Come join us.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AlphaSense Finance team is responsible for efficiently driving the creation of enterprise value by supporting capital allocation decisions across the business. We exist to help the company make intelligent, data-driven decisions through financial analysis; scenario modeling; tracking, interpreting and disseminating key performance indicators; and by serving as a critical thought partner to senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Accountant will own key areas of the monthly close including COGS, cost allocations, and various accruals. You will work as part of a growing team at a well-funded growth-stage, pre-IPO tech company with significant opportunities for rapid career advancement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5+ years of accounting experience, preferably at a SaaS or technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelors degree in Accounting or Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a Big 4 or public accounting firm preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self starter who can operate independently and manage multiple deadlines during a fast-paced month end close process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication skills, with the ability to partner with FP&amp;amp;A and other stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced excel skills required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of US GAAP, including accrual accounting, multi-entity, and intercompany accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to usage-based or technology vendor costs a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with NetSuite and FloQast or similar ERP and close management tool preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely and accurate income statement recognition in accordance with US GAAP&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key areas of the monthly COGS close, including cost allocations and related accruals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare monthly accruals and reversals for content, technology, and other vendor costs&lt;/li&gt;
