&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About AlphaSense:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AlphaSense is the AI platform redefining market intelligence and workflow orchestration, trusted by thousands of leading organizations to drive faster, more confident decisions in business and finance. The platform combines domain-specific AI with a vast content universe of over 500 million premium business documents — including equity research, earnings calls, expert interviews, filings, news, and internal proprietary content. Purpose-built for speed, accuracy, and enterprise-grade security, AlphaSense helps teams extract critical insights, uncover market-moving trends, and automate complex workflows with high-quality outputs. With AI solutions like Generative Search, Generative Grid, and Deep Research, AlphaSense delivers the clarity and depth professionals need to navigate complexity and obtain accurate, real-time information quickly. For more information, visit &lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.alpha-sense.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.alpha-sense.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;. Come join us.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Engineering Manager to lead the teams building shared product platforms at AlphaSense. The domain covers two connected areas: the API-first platforms that power multiple product surfaces, integrations, and agentic workflows, and the usage platform that meters and reports AI credit consumption across our product features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Both areas are built as products, not as internal plumbing. That means well-designed APIs, clear contracts, strong reliability guarantees, and a roadmap driven by real product needs. Our consumption platform is business-critical: it underpins how AlphaSense packages, prices, and reports on AI capabilities, so accurate, timely, and auditable metering is a hard requirement rather than an implementation detail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a people-management role. The immediate team is largely based in EMEA/US, so global people management is preferred. You&#39;ll own hiring, growth, delivery, and the operational health of your teams, and you&#39;ll partner closely with Product, Platform, SRE, and Finance/RevOps to set direction. You&#39;ll stay technical enough to hold credible design discussions, review architecture, and push back where it matters, but your leverage comes through the engineers you grow and the systems they own. You&#39;ll work alongside Principal Engineers in long-term technical direction rather than duplicating that work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, grow, and develop a team of backend and platform engineers across the API and usage/consumption areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery: roadmap commitments, execution quality, and predictable outcomes for platforms with many internal and external consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the direction of usage metering and AI credit accounting, including&amp;nbsp;accuracy, auditability, latency, and cost of the metering pipeline itself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product to shape a platform roadmap driven by real product and customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire strong engineers, build a healthy pipeline, and raise the bar with every offer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold API governance, versioning strategy, and backward compatibility, and hold the line on contracts that other teams depend on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operational excellence: SLOs, observability, on-call health, and follow-through on incidents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance, RevOps, and Pricing on consumption models, entitlements, quotas, overages, and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clarity in ambiguous, cross-team problems and break them into work your teams can execute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow senior ICs and tech leads, and make succession and technical ownership explicit&lt;/li&gt;
