&lt;p&gt;Expert Research is AlphaSense&#39;s expert-call and expert-insights business. Customers use it to find experts, run compliant human- or AI-led interviews, and turn those conversations into research they can act on. We&#39;re growing quickly and putting AI at the center of how we build and test.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Staff Quality Engineer, you will be accountable for quality across this portfolio. You&#39;ll set the testing strategy, close the gaps in our most important customer workflows, and help teams ship faster with confidence. You&#39;ll work across several engineering teams, and you&#39;ll do it without a dedicated QE team or manager, so you&#39;ll set direction yourself and bring people along.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the long-term testing strategy for Expert Research, built on &quot;Quality by Design&quot; and &quot;Automation by Default.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close test coverage gaps on our mission-critical and business-critical workflows, such as call scheduling, expert sourcing, compliance, transcript review, and the client and expert portals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and grow scalable E2E automation, and decide what belongs at the unit, component, API, and E2E layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with developers on test planning for new features, so automation is ready as the code is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set quality metrics and release gates that teams can measure and act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test AI-powered features, including AI-led interviews and call synthesis, and help define how we validate their output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools to speed up test design, maintenance, and triage, and show others how.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach engineers on shift-left and quality-by-design practices, influencing without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on E2E automation experience with at least one of Cypress or Playwright, and the willingness to pick up the other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in at least one programming language (such as Ruby, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, Kotlin, or Java), and comfort working in unfamiliar codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent test design skills, including API testing and a deep understanding of testing theory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with unit and component testing frameworks (such as RSpec or Vitest) and a clear view of how the test layers fit together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of using AI tools to speed up software delivery and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of continuous delivery and release gating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD pipeline setup, test management systems (such as Allure TestOps), performance and observability tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to set direction on your own, without a QE team or manager in place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching engineering teams on quality and influencing across multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication with technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
